>H-M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucht</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Heiss</surname><given-names>W-D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical applications of registration and fusion of multimodality brain images from PET, SPECT, CT, and MRI</article-title><source><italic>European Journal of Radiology</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>21</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>174</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8777907</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rubello</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Casara</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiore</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Muzzio</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zonzin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An ectopic mediastinal parathyroid adenoma accurately located by a single-day imaging protocol of Tc-99m pertechnetate-MIBI subtraction scintigraphy and MIBI-SPECT-computed tomographic image fusion</article-title><source><italic>Clinical Nuclear Medicine</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>27</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>186</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11852306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hellier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Barillot</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A hierarchical parametric algorithm for deformable multimodal image registration</article-title><source><italic>Computer Methods and Programs in Biomedicine</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>75</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>115</lp